BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Given points in a 2D plane, find the pair with the smallest Euclidean distance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 658 Td (DIVIDE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 644 Td (Sort points by x-coordinate, split into left and right halves, and solve each half) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (    recursively.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 611 Td (COMBINE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597 Td (Let delta be the smaller distance from the two halves. Consider points within delta of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (    the dividing line, ordered by y-coordinate; only a bounded number of following) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (    points need comparison.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 551 Td (DISTANCE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (For points \(x1,y1\) and \(x2,y2\), distance = sqrt\(\(x1-x2\)^2 + \(y1-y2\)^2\). Comparing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (    squared distances avoids square roots during comparisons.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 504 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
